So here I am on the Medusa level with an ascension-worthy elven ranger,
and I am fearing the eels.   I've come so far that I am terrified of
being grabbed by one and sucked down to quick, watery instadeath.

So my plan for dealing with them is simple:  I have the longbow of
artemis and arrows. I will use the telepathy conferred by the artifact
to sight the eels, then fill that location full of arrows. When I run
out of arrows, I'll use a polearm.

So I take my first shot -- miss -- wait! Where did my telepathy go?

It takes a couple of seconds of inventory scan before I realize the
awful truth:  I had mis-keyed.

Rather than FIRING an ARROW at the eel, I THREW the Longbow of Artemis
into the drink!

*Sob sob*  What will Orion say to that?  How in the world could I show
my face in the demigod bar (assuming this ranger made it that far)
knowing that the Longbow was still in the drink?

*Sigh* So I went after it.  Used a ring of polymorph and polymorph
control to change into a xorn, slapped on an amulet of unchanging to
make sure I wouldn't revert back underwater, carefully piled all my
possessions into an oilskin sack -- and went into the water after it.

Took  a couple turns exploring the bottom before my Ranger/Xorn emerged
back into the sunlight, triumphantly carrying the bow of Artemis.

But that is going in my book as the dumbest move of the game, barring
the one that gets me killed (if that happens).

